      "description": "Theodren Collins is an Orc cannery owner with a salesman’s smile, a butcher’s efficiency, and a business model that gets uglier the closer anyone reads the supply ledger. He sells preserved meats, caravan rations, and suspiciously cheap emergency tins through the Brass Concordat while blaming sickness on storage errors, customer weakness, or rival sabotage. Theodren is charming enough to sound offended by accusation and careful enough that proving what went into the cans may matter more than surviving the proof.",
      "settlementAndAncestryTexture": "Vaelyssa is a Village in Ceulrithan, under Confessional State, with low danger, Partial forest, Farming, Deep forest terrain. Local records favor Altruistic, Lawful, Cooperative, Honorable civic habits; common communities include Human, Halfling — Lightfoot Halfling, Halfling — Stout Halfling, Kender, Kithkin. Orc reads through the Human entry of the race compendium, within Humans, Near-Humans, and Mixed Heritage, marked by Nebyrr. The local form is read through Half-Orc (Human + Orc Lineage). Humans are highly adaptable and found in nearly every environment across the world. They are known for their cultural diversity, short generational cycles, and unmatched versatility among mortal races. Table cues: Resourceful, Skillful, Versatile; starting tendency Neutral - Neutral - Neutral - Neutral.",
      "rumors": [
        "Workers say Theodren's smokehouse runs hottest after travelers disappear near the clinic road.",
        "Several bad batches tested positive for black-market ichor and something the inspector refused to name."
      ],
      "plotHooks": [
        "Theodren hires the party to discredit a whistleblower, then the whistleblower offers samples from a locked cellar.",
        "A caravan falls ill after eating Theodren's rations, and the cure depends on identifying what meat was actually preserved."
      ],
